<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Cantabri</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The mountain people of northern Spain whose resistance in the Cantabrian Wars of 29 to 19 BCE brought Augustus himself to Iberia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cantabri lived in the Cantabrian mountains and coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabria">Cantabria</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a> and León, from about the 4th century BCE. They were a Celtic-speaking people organised in clans, living in hillforts.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their mountain economy was based on herding goats and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, acorn bread and limited farming, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> noted customs in which daughters inherited and husbands brought dowries. Their warriors raided the plains and served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>; their cavalry manoeuvre, the Cantabrian circle, was adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. They were never united under a single ruler.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Augustus opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> in 29 BCE, campaigning in person in 26 BCE, but conquest was completed only by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-vipsanius-agrippa">Agrippa</a> in 19 BCE, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportations</a>. The land became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hispania-tarraconensis">Hispania Tarraconensis</a>; the name later reappeared in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-cantabria">Duchy of Cantabria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/>